- Line 83 and line 128: `classify("""NCT00000001: { { shortLabel: "a", title: "Percentage of Participants Achieving an American College of Rheumatology 20 response (primary)", estimandType: "OR", effect: 1 } } NCT00000002: { { shortLabel: "b", title: "Percentage of Participants Achieving an American College of Rheumatology 50 response (primary)", estimandType: "OR", effect: 1 } }""", 0.5)` returns poolable. Consequence: ACR20 and ACR50 are different endpoints, but numeric qualifiers are dropped and shared `acr` forces a merge.

- Line 93: `classify("""NCT00000001: { { shortLabel: "a", title: "Overall Survival (primary)", estimandType: "HR", effect: 0.8 } } NCT00000002: { { shortLabel: "b", title: "Overall Survival (primary)", estimandType: "OR", effect: 0.7 } }""", 0.5)` returns poolable. Consequence: HR and OR are incompatible effect measures, but every non-MD estimand collapses to `"binary"`.

- Line 169: `classify("""{ shortLabel: "a", title: "Progression Free Survival (primary)", estimandType: "HR", effect: 0.8 } { shortLabel: "b", title: "Progression-Free Survival (primary)", estimandType: "HR", effect: 0.9 }""", 0.5)` returns poolable. Consequence: absent trial IDs are converted into distinct synthetic trial IDs, so “no trial key found” becomes evidence of two trials.

- Line 141: `classify("""NCT00000001: { { shortLabel: "a", title: "Fracture incidence (primary)", ci: { low: 0, high: 1 }, estimandType: "MD", md: 1 } } NCT00000002: { { shortLabel: "b", title: "Fracture incidence (primary)", estimandType: "OR", effect: 1 } }""", 0.5)` returns poolable. Consequence: a nested `}` before `estimandType` truncates `rest`, so the MD outcome is parsed as binary and can pool with OR.

